      "explanation": "<p>Consider the point F, the focus of the concave mirror. All rays emanating from F will be reflected back parallel to the principal axis PF. Thus, virtual image F' of the point F is formed at <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 1000 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"221E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kysiwwh6/d4703f82-37af-4c9d-a97b-99c6def0ab83/18b02590-7cfd-11ec-83dd-692f0b81f6a2/file-1kysiwwh7.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kysiwwh6/d4703f82-37af-4c9d-a97b-99c6def0ab83/18b02590-7cfd-11ec-83dd-692f0b81f6a2/file-1kysiwwh7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 68 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kysiwwh6/d4703f82-37af-4c9d-a97b-99c6def0ab83/18b02590-7cfd-11ec-83dd-692f0b81f6a2/file-1kysiwwh7.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kysiwwh6/d4703f82-37af-4c9d-a97b-99c6def0ab83/18b02590-7cfd-11ec-83dd-692f0b81f6a2/file-1kysiwwh7.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kysiwwh6/d4703f82-37af-4c9d-a97b-99c6def0ab83/18b02590-7cfd-11ec-83dd-692f0b81f6a2/file-1kysiwwh7.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kysiwwh6/d4703f82-37af-4c9d-a97b-99c6def0ab83/18b02590-7cfd-11ec-83dd-692f0b81f6a2/file-1kysiwwh7.png?format=png 1500w, https:/